WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.970
[VOCALIZING MUSIC]

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.365
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.300
Jennifer Stole my voice.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.560
But if I get some water.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.360
Let's do it.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.770
Hi, I'm Jennifer Hudson.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.710
And this is The Ultimate
RESPECT Playlist.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.850
The first one is
"Accentuate the Positive."

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.790
She has this amazing super
sweet rendition of that song.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.000
So as the first one.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.260
Next--

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.260
"Georgia," by Emily
King-- autobiographical

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.690
and ambiguous simultaneously.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:35.270
Obviously, "Never Loved A
Man The Way That I Love You."

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.890
Mahalia Jackson singing "Take
My Hand, Precious Lord."

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.500
You cannot have a RESPECT
playlist that does not include

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.470
Mahalia Jackson because
Mahalia Jackson meant so much

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.420
to the Franklin Family
and to Aretha's mom.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.330
"Natural Woman," "Think,"
"Never Loved A Man,"

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.320
I could go on and on.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.010
I'm going to add, "I Want
Magic," Renee Fleming.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.258
Her iconic performance
of "Nessun Dorma."

00:00:56.258 --> 00:00:58.300
That was one of the things
that really influenced

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.500
me to train in Opera.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.410
Curtis Mayfield because there's
something very pimp about him.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.930
"Freddie's Dead," "Pusherman."

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:07.750
The next one I picked is
Nina Simone, "Feeling Good,"

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.140
just because it reminds me of
some of Aretha's jazz and Kirby

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.130
recordings.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.398
Definitely Sam Cooke, "A
Change Is Gonna Come."

00:01:14.398 --> 00:01:15.940
And then, there's
a song that I wrote

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.770
called I took the
"You Outta Me" that

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.470
helps me get rid
of negative energy.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.230
My next vote is "Jolene"
by Dolly Parton.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.060
I just think that she
would have killed it

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.320
if she sang that song.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.620
"Chain of Fools,"
oh, I love that song.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.170
"Ain't No Way" because I
love hitting the high note.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:36.415
[VOCALIZING] I hit it, just
not the key on the piano

00:01:36.415 --> 00:01:37.540
that you're suppose to hit.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:39.940
Of course, Aretha Franklin
singing "Amazing Grace."

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:43.180
My parents would listen to
this at least once a week.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:48.070
I got to go with "RESPECT," one
of the greatest anthems ever

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:48.763
created.

00:01:48.763 --> 00:01:50.680
Like how you do a movie called "RESPECT,"

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:51.980
and you ain't play RESPECT.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:55.240
The R-E-S-P-E-C-T.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.380
And that's the ultimate
RESPECT playlist.

